# What stays out of the repo.
#
# The rule: code and settings go in, media and anything rebuildable stays out. Footage alone is several GB and
# GitHub refuses a file over 100 MB, so pushing it would fail halfway and leave a broken repo.

# source footage and everything made from it
footage/
output/
voiceover/
work/
music/
sheets/

# David's packaged GUI: hundreds of MB of bundled Python, and it is not what we run
app/
*.[eE][xX][eE]
*.dll
CHRH Video/
CHRH Video*/

# Video, audio and images anywhere. The patterns are case-insensitive on purpose: a phone writes .MOV, a
# drone .MP4, an export .Mp4, and git matches patterns case-sensitively even on Windows.
*.[mM][pP]4
*.[mM][oO][vV]
*.[mM][kK][vV]
*.[aA][vV][iI]
*.[mM][pP]3
*.[wW][aA][vV]
*.[mM]4[aAvV]
*.[jJ][pP][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
*.[pP][nN][gG]
*.[gG][iI][fF]
*.[wW][eE][bB][pP]

# model files: the CLIP onnx weights are big and downloadable again
*.onnx
*.bin
*.pt

# python leftovers
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# keys never belong in a repo; they live in environment variables
.env
*.key
secrets*

# windows
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
API Keys.txt
*Keys*.txt
*.zip
API Keys.txt
*Keys*.txt
*.zip
